USER no ledger line behind it, or a server-set time from a harness log call with no logger `sent_at`/`received_at` (the
USER response `Date` header or its `created` epoch). The emitter REFUSES hand times by default: exit 3, kind
USER `hand-time`, every field named with its file:line, nothing written. `--allow-hand-times` writes the record, lists
USER each hand time in `x-plumbline.hand_times[]` and records the allowance in `x-plumbline.allowances.hand_times`. The
USER switch FLAGS hand times; it never verifies them, and it silences nothing else.
USER 
USER RELAYS ARE NOT APPROVALS. A `relay` ledger line is a report of something said elsewhere, never an approval. A
USER buyer approval whose only evidence is a relay line (no `approve --role buyer` ledger line and no buyer entry in
